# The site image is built with the repository root as its context, so without
# this file the whole of node_modules and .git is uploaded to the daemon on
# every build. `dist/` is deliberately not excluded: the demo on the page
# imports it over HTTP, so it has to reach the image.
#
# `.git` is no longer excluded either, and that is deliberate: the sitemap's
# `<lastmod>` dates come from the commit that last touched each source file, so
# the docs stage needs the history. Only the objects and refs travel — about
# ten megabytes here — and none of it reaches the image that is served. The
# build survives without it; site/Dockerfile explains how, and the script then
# dates every page today.
node_modules
.github
.claude
*.tsbuildinfo
site/docs
